# Architecture Plan

## Scope for issues #67-#70
- Fix rope behavior so a pulley scene models two rope sides that actually meet the wheel at tangent contact points.
- Replace visible rope segment bodies with a continuous rope overlay renderer.
- Keep loads inside the simulation viewport through scene bounds, optional camera-follow behavior, and scene layout corrections.
- Add regression smoke tests that exercise the repaired engine headlessly.

## Current module ownership
```text
src/
  lib/simulation/
    pulleys.ts               # rope + pulley construction helpers
    drag-interactions.ts     # pointer/touch/keyboard interaction model
    force-overlay.ts         # force/tension overlay drawing
  components/simulation/
    simulation-canvas.tsx
    simulation-canvas-runtime.tsx
    compare-simulations.tsx
  components/lessons/
    *-sandbox-runtime.tsx    # scene-specific pulley setups used by lessons
  app/routes/
    home-page.tsx            # smoke-demo entry points
  test targets
    src/components/readouts/*.test.ts
    src/app/routes/lesson-page.test.tsx
    src/lib/lessonRegistry.test.ts
```

## Shared types and additions
- Extend `createPulley` return data in `src/lib/simulation/pulleys.ts` to expose:
  - wheel body
  - pulley center
  - radius
  - tangent/contact points for left/right rope branches
  - `attachRope(rope)` API for binding a two-sided rope model to the pulley
- Extend `createRope` to represent:
  - left and right segment collections
  - hidden internal segment bodies
  - branch constraints and anchors
  - render metadata for a custom rope overlay
- Add a lightweight rope-renderer type shared between:
  - `src/lib/simulation/pulleys.ts`
  - `src/components/simulation/simulation-canvas-runtime.tsx`
- Add optional scene/runtime config in `SimulationCanvas` for:
  - static boundary walls/floor
  - camera follow mode
  - extra overlay renderers layered between physics and force overlays

## Design decisions
- Keep Matter.js as the source of truth for rope/load motion; the new rope overlay is visual-only and reads segment positions each frame.
- Model pulley wrap as two rope branches anchored to tangent contact points rather than a single straight rope path through the wheel.
- Hide rope segment circles by default after #68 so scenes render one continuous rope stroke instead of dotted bodies.
- Put viewport protection in the shared simulation runtime, not in each lesson scene, so all current and future scenes inherit the same floor/wall behavior.
- Keep scene-specific initial-position fixes inside the lesson runtime components that own each setup.
- Add headless regression tests around the shared helpers and lesson runtime scenes so #70 guards the exact failures fixed in #67-#69.

## Issue dependency map
1. `#67 Make rope actually wrap around the pulley wheel`
   - foundational change in `src/lib/simulation/pulleys.ts`
   - may require small scene updates in lesson runtime components
2. `#68 Continuous rope renderer`
   - depends on the new rope shape/data from `#67`
   - touches `simulation-canvas-runtime.tsx` plus rope helper metadata
3. `#69 Keep weights inside the viewport`
   - shared runtime changes in `simulation-canvas-runtime.tsx`
   - scene tuning in lesson runtime files after the new rope behavior lands
4. `#70 Regression smoke tests`
   - depends on all three fixes above
   - should cover:
     - load remains inside bounds after stepping the engine
     - rope branch segments stay near pulley contact/circumference

## Recommended implementation order
1. Refactor `createPulley`/`createRope` for two-branch wrap behavior.
2. Update existing lesson scenes to use the repaired pulley/rope helpers.
3. Add continuous rope overlay and hide internal rope bodies.
4. Add shared bounds/camera-follow support in `SimulationCanvas`.
5. Tune initial positions/rope lengths in each scene runtime.
6. Add headless smoke tests for the shared engine and affected lesson scenes.
